An instance can be anything. Script, part, model, etc.

# Instantiation & Initialisation
For module creation Instantiation and initialisation are split.
Instantiation is the process of creation of the component.
Initialisation is the starting of it's logic.

# Models
We use templates for models.
templates contain the default data of a model.
A Cframe is a data structure containing the model's coordinates and angle in 3D.

# Tables
Lua uses extensively tables as the most basic data structure.
an empty table is defined as {}.

# metatables
A metatable is what defines custom behaviors for a table.
__index makes a table search for a key it doesn't have.
This makes tables able to access methods from other tables.
Alike inheritance.
Use setmetatable(destination, origin) to set a metatable.
It returns the metatable we assign it to.

# Events
An event makes several scripts able to communicate in real time through signals.
:Fire(...) will send a signal.
.Event:Connect(function) will catch a fired signal.

## Subscribe, Publish, Topic
A topic is a channel categorising messages.
A pubblisher broadcasts a message with a specific topic.
A Subscriber catches and reacts to the messages from the topic he's listening for.

## BindableEvent
A Bindable event is limited to same-side scripts. (only local or only on the server)

